SUBJECT: follow-up to pull request #295 (merge commit c8cf5f9, "fix(mcp): refuse calls to a provider disabled in config"). That PR made every tool refuse a provider with providers.<name>.enabled: false. It left one gap: when the config file exists but cannot be read, the grok and gemini bridges and the unified server treat every provider as ENABLED, while the openrouter bridge refuses. So a user who disabled a provider and then breaks the JSON gets that provider called again.

PLAN (draft v1)

Goal: when ~/.config/deliberation/config.json exists but cannot be parsed, every provider call fails closed with errorKind "config" and a message naming the file and the parse error, instead of falling back to defaults. A missing config file keeps today's defaults.

1. One shared rule in core/provider.js: configErrorResult(error, configPath) returns { isError: true, errorKind: "config", retryable: false, message: "Deliberation config at <path> could not be read (<error>). Fix the file or move it aside; with no file, the defaults apply." }. "Cannot be read" = the reader returns ok:false: JSON parse failure, and any read error other than ENOENT (EACCES, EISDIR). ENOENT stays ok:true with defaults (unchanged).
2. Unified server (server/mcp/index.js): before any provider dispatch - ask-gpt/ask-gemini/ask-grok/ask-openrouter, ask-one, ask-all, the expert tools, consensus, and consensus-step dispatch_peers - if getConfigError() is non-null, return the config error and call no provider. consensus today only adds a warning ("config not loaded: ..."); that becomes a hard stop. Tools that make no provider call (panel, doctor, analyze, session-get, the dashboard) keep working and report the error.
3. Grok and Gemini bridges: grokConfigBlock()/geminiConfig() today return {} on any config problem. Add a check at the top of grok/grok-reply and gemini/gemini-reply: if the reader result is ok:false, answer errorKind "config" before any xAI request or agy spawn. Other tools in those bridges (grok file listing/cleanup) keep working.
4. OpenRouter bridge: already fails closed with code "config" and the raw reader error; change the text to the shared message so all four surfaces say the same thing.
5. Hot reload: all readers are stat-gated on mtime, so fixing the file clears the error on the next call with no restart. No change needed.
6. Tests (new file test/config-fail-closed.test.js): per surface (unified ask-*, ask-one, consensus-step dispatch_peers, grok bridge, gemini bridge, openrouter bridge): (a) bad JSON -> errorKind config, the message names the path and the parse error, the provider stub is never called; (b) fix the file in place -> the next call succeeds (hot reload); (c) missing file -> defaults, calls go through; (d) EACCES (chmod 000, skipped on Windows and as root) -> errorKind config.
7. Docs: TECHNICAL.md (config load states), SETUP.md (what a typo does), docs/tool-guide.md (errorKind config), README config summary.

Out of scope: schema-validation warnings that do not make the reader fail (unknown keys, bad values the validator replaces with defaults) keep today's warn-and-continue behavior.

