server/mcp/index.js (unified server):
```js
// makeRuntime
const reader = makeConfigReader(resolveConfigPath());
const getConfig = () => (reader.get().resolved || { providers: {}, openrouter: {} });
const getConfigError = () => { const r = reader.get(); return r && r.ok === false ? (r.error || "config load failed") : null; };
// Provider model/reasoningEffort/timeout are read ONCE at startup from getConfig(); a change needs a restart.

// buildServer
const startupConfig = structuredClone(getConfig() || {});
const activeConfig = () => effectiveConfig(getConfig() || {}, startupConfig);
const dispatchConfig = () => runContext.getStore()?.config || activeConfig();

// core/settings.js
function effectiveConfig(cfg, startup) {
  return { ...cfg, providers: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries({ ...startup.providers, ...cfg.providers })
    .map(([name, c]) => [name, { ...(startup.providers?.[name] || {}), enabled: c?.enabled }])) };
}
// So: broken at startup -> providers {} -> every provider enabled. Broken after a good start ->
// cfg.providers is {} -> each provider keeps the enabled flag it had at STARTUP (not the last good edit).

// ask-* tools:
if (!providerEnabled(dispatchConfig(), p.name)) return { content: [{ type: "text", text: JSON.stringify({ result: disabledResult(p.name) }) }] };
// consensus (runConsensus):
const cfgErr = getConfigError(); if (cfgErr) warnings.push(`config not loaded: ${cfgErr}`);  // then dispatches anyway
```

Existing tests: test/provider-disabled.test.js PD1-PD10 cover the disabled flag on every surface and hot reload on the Grok bridge (PD10). No test covers a broken config on any surface.

Context: Deliberation is a local MCP server (plus three standalone bridge MCP servers) that hosts like Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and Gemini CLI start at session start. The config file is optional; first-run users have none. Node 18+, no runtime dependencies.

